<div class="mx-auto max-w-lg px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
  <.header>
    How far away is this screen?
    <:subtitle>
      Nothing a browser reports answers this. Two screens can be the same width and be read
      from arm's length and from three metres, and the answer decides how large everything
      here is drawn — so it is asked rather than guessed at.
    </:subtitle>
  </.header>

  <form action={~p"/surface"} method="post" class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value={get_csrf_token()} />
    <input type="hidden" name="return_to" value={@return_to} />

    <button
      :for={{distance, said, how} <- @choices}
      id={"surface-#{distance}"}
      type="submit"
      name="distance"
      value={distance}
      class={[
        "rounded-lg p-4 text-left min-h-target-pointer",
        "border-[length:var(--sys-border-width-component)] border-border-component",
        "bg-fill-subtle hover:bg-fill-subtle-strong hover:border-border-component-strong",
        "text-on-surface-strong"
      ]}
    >
      <span class="block text-title-sm font-semibold">{said}</span>
      <span class="block text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">{how}</span>
    </button>
  </form>

  <p class="mt-6 text-body-sm text-on-surface-muted">
    This is kept with this browser, not with you, because it is a fact about the screen. You
    can change it whenever you like.
  </p>
</div>
